WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:04.843
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.875 --> 00:08.110
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.145 --> 00:11.714
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.748 --> 00:14.717
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.751 --> 00:18.220
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.255 --> 00:21.624
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.658 --> 00:23.259
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.293 --> 00:24.660
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.694 --> 00:29.932
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:31.201 --> 00:33.235
<i>Previously, on Family Guy...</i>

00:33.270 --> 00:35.237
Hey, who wants to play "Drink the Beer"?

00:35.272 --> 00:37.239
- Right here.
- Heh. You win!

00:37.274 --> 00:39.608
- All right! What do I win?
- Another beer!

00:39.643 --> 00:42.545
<i>More recently, and better,
on Family Guy...</i>

00:42.579 --> 00:45.848
All right, you ready?
All right, one, two, three.

00:45.882 --> 00:47.183
Okay, all right.

00:47.217 --> 00:49.251
- Uh, okay. All right.
- Easy, easy, easy, easy.

00:49.286 --> 00:50.653
Whoa-whoa-whoa-whoa, stop, stop, stop,

00:50.687 --> 00:52.188
- stop, stop, stop, stop, stop.
- What? What? What?

00:52.222 --> 00:53.923
- No, no, no, no. Twist it.
- What? I am.

00:53.957 --> 00:55.925
- No. No, no, no, no. No, no, no, no.
- I... I...

00:55.959 --> 00:57.793
Other way, other way,
you're twisting it the wrong way.

00:57.827 --> 01:01.363
<i>Even more recently, and not
quite as good, on  Family Guy...</i>

01:01.398 --> 01:04.099
Jess is going to live!

01:08.305 --> 01:09.972
Brian, did you hear that?

01:10.006 --> 01:11.273
Mm-hmm.

01:11.308 --> 01:13.275
Stewie, I've got to get out of this.

01:13.310 --> 01:15.477
<i>And now, the current,
better-than-the-pilot-</i>

01:15.512 --> 01:17.479
<i>but-not-as-good- as-Star-Wars-episode</i>

01:17.514 --> 01:19.348
<i>of Family Guy.</i>

01:21.518 --> 01:24.420
Sorry it took us so long
to have dinner together.

01:24.454 --> 01:26.589
Oh, that's okay. You were busy...

01:26.623 --> 01:28.023
being dead.

01:31.027 --> 01:33.329
Did you warn this guy
when he married you

01:33.363 --> 01:35.564
he also married your friends?

01:38.802 --> 01:40.970
I love his laugh!

01:41.004 --> 01:44.406
Ha-ha-ha-ha! Ha-ha-ha-ha!

01:44.441 --> 01:46.041
Ah-ha-ha-ha!

01:50.513 --> 01:53.115
Oh, Meg, you have to babysit
for Stewie Saturday.

01:53.149 --> 01:55.317
- Nope.
- Okay. Chris, you have to do it.

01:55.352 --> 01:56.919
What? That's not fair.

01:56.953 --> 01:59.922
- I have a party to go to.
- Sorry, Meg found pictures

01:59.956 --> 02:02.124
on your father's computer,
and she's blackmailing us.

02:02.158 --> 02:05.261
She can do what she wants
till we get some dirt on her.

02:05.295 --> 02:07.196
I didn't know it was supposed to be hard

02:07.230 --> 02:09.164
before I took the picture.

02:20.644 --> 02:22.511
Oh, hey, Peter. Be with you in a sec.

02:22.545 --> 02:24.680
- I'm burning the place down.
- You got the bedbugs?

02:24.714 --> 02:27.483
That don't make sense. This
isn't the Red Rock Motor Lodge

02:27.517 --> 02:29.184
in Montgomery, Alabama.

02:29.219 --> 02:31.020
Please send the lawsuit to our lawyer,

02:31.054 --> 02:32.788
whose address is below.

02:32.822 --> 02:35.357
That's right, she's also a lawyer.

02:35.392 --> 02:37.493
The mystery deepens.

02:37.527 --> 02:39.094
I don't have bedbugs.
I'm burning it down

02:39.129 --> 02:40.529
so I can fake my own death.

02:40.563 --> 02:42.197
Can you throw me that white fur coat

02:42.232 --> 02:44.199
- filled with HoneyBaked hams?
- What?

02:44.234 --> 02:46.568
I just... I can't take it, Peter.

02:46.603 --> 02:49.238
I thought I could marry Jess,
but it's awful!

02:49.272 --> 02:50.906
I can't live this way!

02:50.940 --> 02:52.207
Hey, relax. You're married now.

02:52.242 --> 02:54.009
You don't have to worry about nothin'.

02:54.044 --> 02:55.377
Everything's done for you.

02:55.412 --> 02:58.013
I mean, I literally don't know
where socks come from.

02:58.048 --> 02:59.848
No idea. Do they come from trees?

02:59.883 --> 03:01.216
From bushes? I don't know.

03:01.251 --> 03:03.052
Get a hole in one, new pair shows up

03:03.086 --> 03:04.520
in my drawer, just like that.

03:04.554 --> 03:07.556
Food, too. I chucked the mustard
onto the front lawn last week.

03:07.590 --> 03:09.091
That night, back in the fridge.

03:09.125 --> 03:10.626
<i>That would be kind of nice.</i>

03:10.660 --> 03:11.960
Listen, stick with me.

03:11.995 --> 03:13.662
We're gonna have a great adventure,

03:13.697 --> 03:16.732
like the astronaut who thinks
the lowest number is three.

03:16.766 --> 03:19.601
<i>And liftoff in five, four,</i>

03:19.636 --> 03:21.170
<i>- three...
- Whoa!</i>

03:21.204 --> 03:23.172
<i>- two, one...
- Oh.</i>

03:23.206 --> 03:26.108
<i>- liftoff.
- Whoa!</i>

03:30.213 --> 03:31.547
This is our spot, Brian.

03:31.581 --> 03:34.183
A place just for married guys
like you and me.

03:34.217 --> 03:35.551
Husbands Restaurant?

03:35.585 --> 03:37.052
I've never seen this place before.

03:37.087 --> 03:39.054
- Is it new?
- Nope. Been here for 30 years.

03:39.089 --> 03:41.223
You just can't see it
until you get married.

03:41.257 --> 03:42.624
Watch. Take your ring off.

03:46.596 --> 03:48.097
- Wow!
- Wearing the ring

03:48.131 --> 03:50.199
also makes you wear giant khaki shorts

03:50.233 --> 03:53.369
with a belt and a lot of keys
rattling around in the pockets.

03:56.473 --> 03:58.607
You're right!

03:58.641 --> 04:00.275
What are all these keys for?

04:00.310 --> 04:01.677
A series of sheds.

04:01.711 --> 04:03.712
I got a lot of sheds back home.

04:03.747 --> 04:05.714
Oh. You have more than one shed?

04:05.749 --> 04:07.349
'Course. You always need an extra shed.

04:07.384 --> 04:10.486
I even got one shed that
just has an extra shed in it.

04:10.520 --> 04:13.422
- You guys talking about sheds?
- Hell yes. I love my sheds.

04:13.456 --> 04:15.457
- Me, too.
- High five on sheds.

04:15.492 --> 04:16.725
Sheds!

04:16.760 --> 04:18.293
Sheds...

04:18.328 --> 04:22.131
sheds... sheds... sheds...

04:25.301 --> 04:27.770
Are those really Tom Arnold's
sweatpants in that frame?

04:27.804 --> 04:29.838
Yep. That's the Husbands wall of heroes.

04:29.873 --> 04:32.107
There are a lot of fat guys here.

04:32.142 --> 04:33.942
Well, yeah, Brian.
Every man's true weight

04:33.977 --> 04:36.145
is at least 20 pounds heavier
than how they look.

04:36.179 --> 04:38.914
You know how much energy
it takes to hold all that in?

04:38.948 --> 04:40.315
You can finally let go.

04:40.350 --> 04:42.584
Just relax. Exhale for once.

04:42.619 --> 04:44.620
Exhale like you never have to attract

04:44.654 --> 04:46.755
a pretty woman ever again.

04:52.362 --> 04:54.663
Wow, that feels amazing.

04:54.697 --> 04:56.899
Now, let's order some food.
I'm starving.

04:56.933 --> 04:59.334
Nice to meet you, Starving. I'm Brian.

05:13.116 --> 05:16.351
Oh, looks like they really
want me to come to that party.

05:16.386 --> 05:19.488
- We're gonna have to go.
- You... you have a pager?

05:19.522 --> 05:21.323
- Yeah.
- You get paged?

05:21.357 --> 05:23.025
Yeah, that's how a pager works.

05:23.059 --> 05:24.993
Why don't you just get a phone?

05:25.028 --> 05:27.696
Um, you mean one of your
government tracking devices?

05:27.730 --> 05:29.698
No, thanks. I'm using a pager.

05:29.732 --> 05:31.700
"Oh, you're looking at your steps?"

05:31.734 --> 05:34.169
No, the government's
watching where you're going.

05:34.204 --> 05:37.172
It's not nap time, Stewie. Wake up.

05:37.207 --> 05:39.708
All right, we're out of here.

05:39.742 --> 05:41.577
Okay, Stewie's going to the party.

05:41.611 --> 05:44.046
- Yeah, but where's Chris going?
- I have no idea!

05:44.080 --> 05:45.881
He's completely off the grid!

05:45.915 --> 05:48.517
Damn it! He can't hide forever.

05:51.087 --> 05:53.722
Where are you?

06:02.065 --> 06:04.032
Boy, this really is a high school party.

06:04.067 --> 06:06.668
Complete with the popular kid
who's clearly going to die

06:06.703 --> 06:08.504
in a car accident tonight.

06:08.538 --> 06:10.672
Hey, Jagger, can you
help out at the soup kitchen

06:10.707 --> 06:13.475
- tomorrow at noon?
- Sure. I should be alive then.

06:13.510 --> 06:15.043
Yeah, he gone.

06:16.079 --> 06:17.846
I see we're smoking.

06:17.881 --> 06:19.681
We're not smoking. We're vaping.

06:19.716 --> 06:22.017
- What's the difference?
- Smoking is for losers.

06:22.051 --> 06:23.819
Vaping is for douchebags.

06:23.853 --> 06:25.821
Aw. I want to be a douchebag.

06:25.855 --> 06:27.689
Do you own 19 hats?

06:27.724 --> 06:31.360
I only have one, but it's a
Stussy hat with a flat brim.

06:31.394 --> 06:32.761
Have a seat.

06:38.801 --> 06:40.869
Whoo-hoo, it's delightful!

06:40.904 --> 06:43.171
Chris! Chris, isn't this cool?

06:43.206 --> 06:46.174
Stewie, don't say my name!
There's an Alexa in here!

06:47.443 --> 06:49.111
Sir, we have eyes on Chris.

06:49.145 --> 06:51.146
He's at a douchebag vaping party.

06:51.180 --> 06:55.117
Sooner or later, they all get sloppy.

07:01.457 --> 07:03.258
I got to say, Bri, the guys at Husbands

07:03.293 --> 07:04.693
are a little worried about you.

07:04.727 --> 07:06.094
They said you had four

07:06.129 --> 07:08.130
Scott Peterson
fish sandwiches yesterday.

07:09.966 --> 07:11.400
Fireball?

07:11.434 --> 07:13.702
No, because I'm not a Skidmore freshman

07:13.736 --> 07:15.904
at a Lake George share-house.

07:15.939 --> 07:17.806
Or am I?

07:20.009 --> 07:21.443
Man, Skidmore's the best!

07:21.477 --> 07:23.478
You said it, Pete. Race you to the raft?

07:23.513 --> 07:24.680
You're on!

07:24.714 --> 07:26.148
Yeah, let's go!

07:26.182 --> 07:28.684
<i>But the water was too shallow.</i>

07:28.718 --> 07:31.286
<i>Bryce broke his neck
and never walked again.</i>

07:31.321 --> 07:33.455
<i>This put an end to off-campus drinking</i>

07:33.489 --> 07:35.290
<i>and lake house rentals.</i>

07:35.325 --> 07:36.491
<i>I was just fine.</i>

07:36.526 --> 07:38.293
<i>I landed on Bryce.</i>

07:39.996 --> 07:41.964
He's starting to smell.

07:41.998 --> 07:43.432
He needs a bath.

07:43.466 --> 07:45.367
He doesn't like baths.

07:45.401 --> 07:48.103
And I see you lost the alcohol argument.

07:48.137 --> 07:49.805
Can't you hear them talking about you?

07:49.839 --> 07:52.174
Yeah. I'm a dog, I can hear everything.

07:52.208 --> 07:55.143
<i>By the way, the Stranger Things
monster just farted.</i>

07:55.178 --> 07:58.647
Whew! Must have been
that fat chick I ate.

07:58.681 --> 08:01.516
- Time for dinner, guys.
- Awesome. I'm starving.

08:02.518 --> 08:04.319
Oh!

08:04.354 --> 08:05.654
Oh...

08:05.688 --> 08:07.356
Holy crap! Brian, you okay?

08:12.528 --> 08:14.229
Keep it down up there!

08:15.865 --> 08:17.933
Holy crap, Hal, what's wrong with you?

08:17.967 --> 08:20.202
You love it.

08:26.701 --> 08:27.881
How does it look, Doc?

08:27.883 --> 08:30.151
I'm sorry to say you have hip dysplasia.

08:30.185 --> 08:31.652
What's that?

08:31.687 --> 08:33.754
I'm not re what dysplasia is,
but I do know

08:33.789 --> 08:36.324
you don't often see a "Y"
that far up in a word.

08:36.358 --> 08:38.259
I took the liberty
of X-raying my own hip

08:38.293 --> 08:40.494
to show you what
a normal one looks like.

08:40.529 --> 08:42.963
Why does it look like there's
a Batmobile in your colon?

08:42.998 --> 08:44.465
Just keep your eyes on the hips.

08:44.499 --> 08:45.866
So, what's the next step?

08:45.901 --> 08:48.803
I was hoping, whenever the
Bat-Signal goes up in the sky,

08:48.837 --> 08:51.305
- this thing will just drive out.
- Uh, no. For Brian.

08:51.340 --> 08:53.507
Ah. Well, wouldn't hurt
to lose some weight.

08:53.542 --> 08:56.344
And he won't be able to walk
until his hip heals.

08:56.378 --> 08:58.512
He'll need someone to take care of him.

08:58.547 --> 08:59.947
I'll take care of him.

08:59.981 --> 09:02.683
<i>Like you took care of me
when I was sick.</i>

09:02.718 --> 09:04.819
Come back in a week,
we can check your pfft-pfft.

09:04.853 --> 09:05.986
What is that?

09:06.021 --> 09:07.788
That's the sound
a blood pressure machine makes.

09:07.823 --> 09:09.857
I do impressions
for the doctor talent show.

09:09.891 --> 09:11.659
Do you know what this is?

09:11.693 --> 09:13.794
Braaap! Braaap!

09:13.829 --> 09:15.529
An MRI?

09:15.564 --> 09:18.132
Yes! Adding that to my set.

09:22.971 --> 09:24.505
Oh, my God.

09:24.539 --> 09:26.674
- Where there's smoke, there's...
- Just me vaping.

09:26.708 --> 09:28.809
Stewie, if Mom and Dad
see you with that thing,

09:28.844 --> 09:29.977
they'll kill me.

09:30.011 --> 09:31.212
Get rid of it!

09:31.246 --> 09:33.047
No way. It's awesome. Watch this.

09:39.588 --> 09:41.555
I'm not good at the football part.

09:41.590 --> 09:43.557
It smells like raspberry.

09:43.592 --> 09:45.860
Yeah. It's basically the same
as eating fruit.

09:45.894 --> 09:48.929
- Vaping isn't bad for you?
- It can't be bad for you

09:48.964 --> 09:50.998
if Stephen Dorff gave up acting for it.

09:51.032 --> 09:53.567
It does seem like they're
making it for kids.

09:53.602 --> 09:56.337
This flavor is... "baby formula."

09:56.371 --> 09:58.038
Let me try.

10:00.075 --> 10:01.409
Yummy.

10:01.443 --> 10:02.843
Watch this.

10:07.149 --> 10:09.183
<i>Like the movie The Ring.</i>

10:09.217 --> 10:10.551
Awesome!

10:14.256 --> 10:15.589
Come back here, you.

10:16.758 --> 10:19.226
Giggity, giggity, crabbity, giggity.

11:35.637 --> 11:37.137
E-liquid, please.

11:37.172 --> 11:39.073
Anything that tastes like
a Fruit Roll-Up.

11:39.107 --> 11:40.274
Good, all good.

11:40.308 --> 11:41.342
- Good.
- All good.

11:41.376 --> 11:42.643
No worries, all good?

11:42.677 --> 11:44.311
- We're good.
- Good, all good.

11:44.346 --> 11:45.346
Here you go.

11:45.380 --> 11:46.480
You good? You all good?

11:46.515 --> 11:47.982
- All good here.
- Yep, we're good.

11:48.016 --> 11:49.950
Good, all good.

11:49.985 --> 11:52.653
This whole vaping thing
was a very smart move.

11:52.687 --> 11:54.955
It tastes great
and I don't feel violently ill

11:54.990 --> 11:57.191
as long as some of this vapor
is in my lungs.

11:57.225 --> 11:59.260
Plus, when you wake at night shaking

11:59.294 --> 12:01.128
because you haven't had any
in three hours,

12:01.162 --> 12:03.230
it's so easy to vape more.

12:03.265 --> 12:05.199
Let's face it, this is
the most fun we've had

12:05.233 --> 12:08.702
since Mom got hooked on coffee
and bought that Alpuccino maker.

12:08.737 --> 12:12.239
Hoo-ah!

12:15.844 --> 12:18.345
Thank you for having us over for dinner.

12:18.380 --> 12:21.482
Sometimes it's been difficult to cook

12:21.516 --> 12:23.884
with all the other things
I have to do for Brian.

12:23.919 --> 12:26.086
Oh, don't listen to her, I'm so easy.

12:26.121 --> 12:28.022
I do have to go to the bathroom, though.

12:30.392 --> 12:32.192
Jess really has been amazing.

12:33.695 --> 12:36.230
She even set up surgery for me
to have my hip fixed.

12:38.266 --> 12:40.134
Uhp, don't get fooled.

12:41.403 --> 12:42.870
I don't know what I'd do without her.

12:42.904 --> 12:45.039
I think I've really found true love.

12:45.073 --> 12:47.541
Well, that's lovely.

12:47.576 --> 12:49.677
You know, I don't think
we've said grace yet.

12:49.711 --> 12:51.211
- Oh, yeah.
- Bless us, oh Lord,

12:51.246 --> 12:52.880
for these thy gifts,
which we are about to receive.

12:52.914 --> 12:54.748
Get out of there, Mountain Dew.

12:58.753 --> 13:00.554
I'm here for Brian Griffin.

13:00.589 --> 13:01.755
Well, this is it, Jess.

13:01.790 --> 13:03.557
See you after my hip surgery.

13:03.592 --> 13:05.559
He won't be needing this anymore.

13:05.594 --> 13:06.694
Thanks.

13:06.728 --> 13:08.162
Good-bye, Brian.

13:08.196 --> 13:09.930
You mean "see you soon," right?

13:09.965 --> 13:11.565
Wait, why won't I need my collar?

13:14.636 --> 13:16.604
So, what's this?

13:16.638 --> 13:18.238
Kind of like a pre-op?

13:18.273 --> 13:20.107
Are all these dogs having hip surgery?

13:21.142 --> 13:22.576
Where do you think you are?

13:22.611 --> 13:25.212
This isn't a doctor's office,
this is the pound.

13:25.246 --> 13:26.747
You're being euthanized.

13:26.781 --> 13:29.383
What? Jess is having me put down?

13:29.417 --> 13:31.752
Oh, my God, this can't be happening!

13:31.786 --> 13:34.355
Did you also eat a kid?

13:42.521 --> 13:44.255
Look, there's been a horrible mistake.

13:44.290 --> 13:45.657
You've got the wrong dog.

13:45.691 --> 13:48.359
Says right here I got
to euthanize Brian Griffin,

13:48.394 --> 13:50.161
and you're him.

13:50.195 --> 13:52.397
You wouldn't kill
a singing dog, would you?

13:52.431 --> 13:54.666
<i>Hello, my baby, hello, my honey</i>

13:54.700 --> 13:57.001
<i>Hello, my ragtime gal.</i>

14:11.383 --> 14:15.086
Oh, now you're getting
euthanized for sure.

14:22.861 --> 14:24.262
Hi, honey.

14:24.296 --> 14:26.364
Mommy needs money for scratchers.

14:26.398 --> 14:29.767
What the... what kind
of brazen thievery is this?

14:31.470 --> 14:33.371
Where'd you get this?

14:33.405 --> 14:35.373
Chris Griffin! You get in here!

14:36.475 --> 14:37.709
What is this?

14:37.743 --> 14:39.610
Um... robot penis?

14:39.645 --> 14:41.546
Seriously, I'm absolutely
jonesing right now,

14:41.580 --> 14:42.780
so give it back.

14:42.815 --> 14:44.082
I know what this is. I watch Bravo.

14:44.116 --> 14:45.450
- I'm not doing it.
- You are too young

14:45.484 --> 14:46.884
- to be doing this.
- Maybe it's his and he's just

14:46.919 --> 14:48.252
- too dumb to hide it.
- And if that's not bad enough,

14:48.287 --> 14:49.787
you leave it out for Stewie
to get his hands on it?

14:49.822 --> 14:51.923
I don't know, Mom,
I'm not my brother's keeper.

14:51.957 --> 14:54.158
- He's just a baby.
- Babies are stupid like that!

14:54.193 --> 14:55.426
I'm taking it...

14:55.461 --> 14:57.762
and you are grounded, mister.

14:57.796 --> 15:00.398
Now look what you did,
you little son of a bitch.

15:00.432 --> 15:01.466
She has my vaporizer.

15:01.500 --> 15:02.734
You have to get it back.

15:02.768 --> 15:04.235
That's your problem.

15:04.269 --> 15:06.938
You lost your vape pen,
I didn't lose mine.

15:06.972 --> 15:09.674
Well, I guess you win.

15:20.686 --> 15:22.987
Hey.

15:36.168 --> 15:38.403
Oh, tastes so good, like skin berries.

15:38.437 --> 15:40.371
I'm alive with pleasure.

15:50.616 --> 15:52.550
It's possible we've taken this too far.

15:52.584 --> 15:55.353
I'll just go down and get yours back.

15:56.955 --> 16:00.024
I will never forget this day.

16:03.061 --> 16:05.229
Mom, I need to talk to you.

16:05.264 --> 16:07.598
Technically, that was not my vape pen,

16:07.633 --> 16:10.701
but I do need it back because
it belongs to a friend of mine.

16:10.736 --> 16:12.537
We accidentally switched jackets,

16:12.571 --> 16:15.106
<i>not unlike that episode
of The Brady Bunch when Greg...</i>

16:17.142 --> 16:20.445
Oh, damn it, Chris, why do your
lies have to take so damn long?

16:20.479 --> 16:22.380
You're smoking the vape pen?

16:22.414 --> 16:24.182
No, I'm sneaking a real cigarette

16:24.216 --> 16:26.284
like frustrated mothers
are supposed to do.

16:26.318 --> 16:28.352
You're such a hypocrite!

16:28.387 --> 16:29.954
At least vaping is healthy.

16:29.988 --> 16:31.522
Oh, don't be an idiot.

16:31.557 --> 16:34.025
Vaping is just as bad,
and you look like a douchebag.

16:34.059 --> 16:36.327
No, I don't. I look cool.

16:36.361 --> 16:37.962
Go ahead.

16:37.996 --> 16:39.530
Hold it to your mouth.

16:42.468 --> 16:45.603
Oh, my God, I'm a douchebag.

16:48.774 --> 16:50.007
It's okay, Chris.

16:50.042 --> 16:51.876
Your secret's safe with me.

17:05.924 --> 17:07.191
Hey, what's up, Jess?

17:07.226 --> 17:08.693
I came to see how Brian's...

17:08.727 --> 17:10.094
Hoo-ah!

17:10.128 --> 17:12.129
Sorry, I'm just making an Alpuccino.

17:12.164 --> 17:13.498
Oh.

17:13.532 --> 17:14.765
Well, anyway, I was just wondering...

17:14.800 --> 17:16.367
Hoo-ah!

17:16.401 --> 17:18.035
Sorry, my mom wanted one, too.

17:18.070 --> 17:19.403
Oh, that's-that's fine.

17:19.438 --> 17:21.038
- So is Brian...
- Can I get you one?

17:21.073 --> 17:22.139
Uh, sure.

17:22.174 --> 17:23.374
Is Brian going to, uh...

17:23.408 --> 17:24.909
Hoo-ah!

17:24.943 --> 17:26.244
When is Brian coming back?

17:26.278 --> 17:27.378
Oh, never.

17:27.412 --> 17:28.713
I'm having him euthanized.

17:28.747 --> 17:30.081
Euthanized?

17:30.115 --> 17:31.449
Oh, my God!

17:38.323 --> 17:39.690
Come on, come on.

17:51.103 --> 17:53.971
Euthanize, euthanize, euthanize...

17:57.276 --> 17:58.476
Oh, my God!

17:58.510 --> 18:00.011
I got to do something!

18:05.584 --> 18:08.553
Damn it. Now I have to do that
with every dictionary here.

18:08.587 --> 18:10.788
Hold on, Brian, hold on.

18:16.461 --> 18:18.396
Don't worry, buddy. I'm on my way.

18:26.538 --> 18:30.408
I'm warning you, if you kill me,
the Internet's gonna freak out.

18:35.647 --> 18:37.448
Please, it can't end like this.

18:37.482 --> 18:39.116
There has to be something I can do.

18:39.151 --> 18:41.018
Well, for 200 bucks, I'll strangle you

18:41.053 --> 18:44.255
with my bare hands and stare
into your eyes as you die.

18:44.289 --> 18:46.157
What? I'm not paying for that.

18:46.191 --> 18:47.758
I meant I'll pay you.

18:47.793 --> 18:49.794
Stop! That's my dog!

18:49.828 --> 18:51.162
Oh, Peter, thank God.

18:51.196 --> 18:52.730
You got here just in time.

18:52.764 --> 18:54.865
You want to make $200?

18:54.900 --> 18:56.133
I do.

18:56.168 --> 19:00.538
It's... beautiful.

19:03.208 --> 19:04.609
What the hell are you doing here?

19:04.643 --> 19:06.043
Brian, I can explain.

19:06.078 --> 19:08.512
Explain what? How you brought me
here to have me killed?

19:08.547 --> 19:09.847
Well, you're no better.

19:09.881 --> 19:11.515
You could have saved my life
in the restaurant,

19:11.550 --> 19:13.417
but you let me choke to death.

19:13.452 --> 19:15.853
Okay, fine.
I probably could have done more

19:15.887 --> 19:17.188
to save your life.

19:17.222 --> 19:19.357
I was just so unhappy
being married, I...

19:19.391 --> 19:23.027
I guess I felt letting you Che
was my only way out.

19:23.061 --> 19:24.328
God, that sounds awful.

19:24.363 --> 19:25.763
Maybe I did deserve to die.

19:25.797 --> 19:28.399
W-Well, and I should've kept
taking care of you,

19:28.433 --> 19:30.868
instead of bringing you here
to have you killed.

19:30.902 --> 19:34.772
Maybe I deserve to be
with someone who let me die.

19:34.806 --> 19:38.009
Maybe we deserve each other.

19:38.043 --> 19:40.544
It does seem like we're meant
for each other.

19:40.579 --> 19:44.048
I mean, gosh, maybe that's what
true marriage is...

19:44.082 --> 19:46.150
two people who want each other to die.

19:46.184 --> 19:47.818
Now you're getting it.

19:47.853 --> 19:50.454
So much beauty.

19:55.434 --> 19:57.633
Oh, Brian, I'm sorry that Jess died

19:57.635 --> 19:58.935
during the commercial break,

19:58.970 --> 20:01.338
but it was a very nice funeral service.

20:01.372 --> 20:03.306
Yeah, it's sad.

20:03.341 --> 20:06.509
She was the love of my life,
my heart, my...

20:06.544 --> 20:07.577
Hoo-ah!

20:07.612 --> 20:10.680
I took that from her apartment.

20:10.715 --> 20:13.183
So, Chris, I hear
you been doing some vaping.

20:13.217 --> 20:14.651
So douchey.

20:14.685 --> 20:16.386
Mom, you told him?

20:16.420 --> 20:18.588
- We had a deal.
- Thanks a lot, Peter.

20:18.623 --> 20:20.357
You promised you wouldn't say anything.

20:20.391 --> 20:21.992
Oh, I'm supposed to keep your secret

20:22.026 --> 20:23.994
after you lied to me
about sneaking cigarettes?

20:24.028 --> 20:26.496
What the hell, Chris? You told him, too?

20:26.530 --> 20:28.632
- No, I didn't.
- Brian told me.

20:28.666 --> 20:31.134
Are you serious, Peter? You said
you wouldn't say anything.

20:31.168 --> 20:32.702
I promised Meg I wouldn't tell anyone.

20:32.737 --> 20:34.871
Oh, good job with that, dick.

20:34.905 --> 20:36.706
Chris, the only reason I told him

20:36.741 --> 20:38.475
was he promised he'd keep
his mouth shut.

20:38.509 --> 20:40.010
Oh, nice job, Chris.

20:40.044 --> 20:41.411
I should've known not to trust someone

20:41.445 --> 20:42.879
who kisses his own brother.

20:42.913 --> 20:44.814
What? Wh-Who told you that?

20:44.849 --> 20:46.783
- Don't look at me.
- Meg told me.

20:46.817 --> 20:49.819
How does it feel, Meg,
you frigging town crier?

20:49.854 --> 20:51.921
<i>- You're such a bitch.
- She's a bitch?</i>

20:51.956 --> 20:54.090
<i>Meg, you said you
wouldn't tell Stewie's secret.</i>

20:54.125 --> 20:55.558
Stewie, you told Dad?

20:55.593 --> 20:57.060
I had to get it off my chest.

20:57.094 --> 20:58.395
I didn't think he'd understand me.

20:58.429 --> 21:00.930
I understand pieces now and then.

21:00.931 --> 21:03.937
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv